# espix timezone.
#
# A POSIX TZ string, NOT a zoneinfo name. Linux puts "Africa/Johannesburg" in
# this file and keeps the rules in /etc/localtime; espix ships no tzdata -- the
# database is megabytes -- so the rules live here in the string itself.
#
#   UTC0                         no offset, no DST (the "0" is required)
#   SAST-2                       UTC+2, no DST  (note the sign is inverted)
#   GMT0BST,M3.5.0/1,M10.5.0     UK, with DST
#   EST5EDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0       US eastern, with DST
#
# The sign is backwards from what you expect: the number is what you add to
# local time to get UTC, so UTC+2 is written -2. That is POSIX, not a typo.
#
# `timedatectl set-timezone <string>` rewrites this file.
UTC0
